From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:57:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: gtactive3wifi: kernel: sensors fragment

The BCM4775 sensor-hub driver (src/linux drv/shub2) as a module:
accelerometer, light and proximity for iio-sensor-proxy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh | 2 +-
 contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/sensors.config       | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/sensors.config

diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh
index 29247bf..fb9092f 100755
--- a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ OUTCFG=$APORT/config-postmarketos-exynos9810.aarch64
 LOCK=$ROOT/build/kbuild.lock
 BUILDER=${BUILDER:-gta3-pkgbuilder}
 # device fragments, applied in this order
-DEVFRAGS="gtactive3wifi.config virt.config camera.config pm.config hwgaps.config performance.config"
+DEVFRAGS="gtactive3wifi.config virt.config camera.config pm.config hwgaps.config performance.config sensors.config"
 
 podman image exists "$BUILDER" ||
 	podman build -t "$BUILDER" -f "$HERE/../pkgbuilder.Containerfile" "$HERE/.."
diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/sensors.config b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/sensors.config
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8553679
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/sensors.config
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# Sensors (src/linux drv/shub2): accelerometer, ambient light and
+# proximity behind the sensor hub of the BCM4775 GNSS chip on SPI20. The
+# driver downloads the hub application (the owner's Samsung firmware,
+# samsung/gtactive3wifi/bbd/bcm_sensorhub_a1.patch) and exposes standard
+# IIO devices for iio-sensor-proxy (auto-rotate, auto-brightness).
+CONFIG_IIO_BCM4775_SHUB=m
